The organisation sets security targets each year, follows the controls through the year, and the management reviews the ISMS at least once a year.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs an ISMS. NIS2 requires policies and procedures to assess the effectiveness of the cybersecurity risk-management measures. The metrics are in the control "Measure the effectiveness of security", and the management review handles their results.

== How to implement

Set the security targets of the year in the security targets register. Follow the annual wheel: each internal control has a review month, and the owner reviews the control in that month. Hold a management review at least once a year.

